## 8. Disclaimer of Warranties; Status of the Software; High-Risk Use

**8.1 Disclaimer.** To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Software is provided "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any warranty of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, non-infringement or accuracy, and including any warranty that the Software is secure, error-free or uninterrupted. Licensee assumes all risk of selecting, installing, running and relying on the Software.

**8.2 What the Software is.** Synthyrion Core L5 is a capability-based microkernel written in Rust, with versions for x86-64 (Intel and AMD), AArch32 (32-bit Arm), AArch64 (64-bit Arm) and RISC-V 64. Hardware evidence exists for x86-64; the AArch32, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 versions run in emulation (QEMU) only. It is under active development. Its feature status is published at synthyrion.com, with the strength of each piece of evidence (tested, bounded, panic-free or functionally proven; on host, virtual machine or hardware). It has no safety, security or government certification. There is no whole-kernel functional-correctness proof. It is not FIPS 140-3 validated.

**8.3 High-risk use.** The Software is not certified for, and must not be relied on in, any life-, safety- or mission-critical system (including medical devices, aircraft, vehicles, nuclear facilities, weapons or critical infrastructure) unless a separate written agreement with Synthyrion expressly covers that use.

**8.4 No support.** Synthyrion has no support obligation, service levels, response times or uptime commitments under this Licence.

