**9.4 Basis of the bargain.** The Software is offered free of charge in reliance on Sections 8 and 9.

## 10. Termination and Notice-and-Cure

**10.1 Notice and cure (non-wilful breaches).** For a non-monetary, inadvertent breach (for example an accidentally omitted copyright notice, an attribution error, or a late certificate under Section 6.2), Synthyrion will give written notice. If Licensee cures the breach within thirty (30) calendar days after receiving the notice, all rights continue. This Section 10.1 does not apply to any export or sanctions violation (Section 11.6), to removing or altering a Fingerprint or Licence File, or to a breach of Section 3.4(d).

**10.2 Immediate termination.** This Licence ends immediately and automatically, without a cure period, on (a) intentional failure to report a Threshold Event; (b) wilful evasion of the commercial licensing requirement; (c) use or distribution past the Conversion Deadline; (d) any export or sanctions violation, or a failure to stop unauthorised sanctioned access on discovery; (e) removal or alteration of a Fingerprint or Licence File; or (f) the patent-litigation event in Section 3.12 (as to the patent licences).

**10.3 Suspension.** Synthyrion may suspend access to downloads and paid services immediately where Section 11.5 allows.

**10.4 Effect of termination.** On termination Licensee must stop reproducing, compiling, executing, linking, distributing and commercially using the Software and destroy all copies in its possession or control.

**10.5 Units already shipped; recipients.** End customers who received the Software in good faith inside Licensee's products, and other recipients who received it in good faith under Section 3.6, keep their own licence from Synthyrion, and may keep running the copies they have, as long as they comply with this Licence and are not Restricted Parties.

**10.6 Survival.** Sections 2, 6.4 to 6.7, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13 and 14 survive termination.

## 11. Export Controls and Sanctions

**11.1 Export notice.** The Software contains encryption and is subject to the U.S. Export Administration Regulations (EAR). Its export classification is pending; until it is confirmed, treat it as ECCN 5D002. See SYN-L5-DOC-20 and the Export Notice (W8).

**11.2 Prohibited transfers.** Licensee will not export, re-export, transfer or provide the Software, directly or indirectly:

(a) to any country or region subject to comprehensive U.S. sanctions or embargo or website access block (as of drafting: Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, and the Crimea, Sevastopol, so-called Donetsk People's Republic and Luhansk People's Republic regions of Ukraine; the list changes and the current OFAC/BIS list controls);

(b) to any person or entity on a U.S. restricted-party list, including the OFAC SDN List, the BIS Entity List, Denied Persons List, Unverified List and Military End-User List (the Consolidated Screening List), or any entity owned 50 percent or more by one or more such persons;

(c) for any military end use or to a military end user where the EAR restricts it (15 C.F.R. § 744.21), for any military-intelligence end use or end user (15 C.F.R. § 744.22), or for nuclear, chemical, biological or missile end uses (15 C.F.R. Part 744); or

(d) to Russia or Belarus, or in violation of the EAR's restrictions on Russia and Belarus (15 C.F.R. Part 746).

**11.3 Representations.** Licensee represents and warrants that it is not located in, organised under the laws of, or ordinarily resident in a Restricted Jurisdiction, is not a Restricted Party, and is not owned or controlled by one. Licensee is responsible for obtaining any government authorisation it needs; this does not relieve Synthyrion of its own obligations as exporter.

**11.4 Screening and information.** Licensee will re-screen every recipient before redistributing the Software (Section 3.4), and will give Synthyrion end-use and end-user information on request and notify it of changes. Synthyrion blocks downloads from restricted jurisdictions and records each download (Section 3.8). Paid purchases are screened against the Consolidated Screening List at checkout.

**11.5 Suspension and termination.** Synthyrion may suspend or terminate access immediately, without a cure period, if it believes a violation of this Section 11 has occurred.

**11.6 No cure.** Export violations are never "administrative breaches". Section 10.1 never applies to them.

**11.7 Records.** Synthyrion keeps screening, acceptance and download records for ten (10) years.

